<section id="section-14">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">14</span>
    <h2>Data Storytelling &amp; Narrative</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-intro">Effective data visualisation tells a story that guides the reader through information. A coherent structure and logical flow help users follow the data and understand its implications. Good narrative aids comprehension and supports decision-making — without manipulating the conclusion.</p>

  <div class="grid-3 mb-lg">
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 01</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">State the insight in the title</h4>
      <p class="text-sm mb-xs">The chart title should answer the question the chart poses — not describe the chart type.</p>
      <div class="code-snippet">
        <div class="text-pass">✅ "APAC overtook EMEA in Q4"</div>
        <div class="text-fail mt-xxs">❌ "Revenue by region, Q4"</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 02</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">Annotate the moment that matters</h4>
      <p class="text-sm mb-xs">Guide the reader to the insight with a short annotation at the right data point — not a paragraph of surrounding text.</p>
      <div class="code-snippet">
        <div class="text-pass">✅ "Policy change" at the inflection point</div>
        <div class="text-fail mt-xxs">❌ Three paragraphs below the chart</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 03</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">Layer complexity progressively</h4>
      <p class="text-sm mb-xs">Start with the headline number. Let the reader go deeper through interaction or supplementary charts. Never front-load complexity.</p>
      <div class="code-snippet">
        <div class="text-pass">✅ Hero stat → trend → breakdown</div>
        <div class="text-fail mt-xxs">❌ Dense multi-series with no entry point</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 04</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">Embed text and data together</h4>
      <p class="text-sm mb-xs">Written narrative and charts should work together — not sit in separate sections. Key numbers in text should be emphasised inline.</p>
      <div class="code-snippet">Tobacco use is projected to <u>fall by 30 points</u> from 49.6% to <strong class="text-orange">19.6%</strong> by 2025.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 05</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">Always cite the source</h4>
      <p class="text-sm mb-xs">Every chart must include a data source and data date. This is a transparency requirement, not optional. Use a smaller typographic weight below the chart.</p>
      <div class="code-snippet mono-sm text-muted">Source: ONS · Data as of Q3 2025</div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-sm card--accent-slate">
      <div class="kicker kicker--slate">STEP 06</div>
      <h4 class="card-title-sm">Maintain narrative integrity</h4>
      <p class="text-sm">The story the chart tells must be the story the data supports. Avoid selecting date ranges or scales that make a trend appear more dramatic than it is. The reader's trust is the product.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
